    "result_text": "`BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field derived from the owner's city.\n\n**Changes (2 files):**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added one `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", ...)` inline expression to the existing `toOwnerDto` method, using a Java switch expression: `Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`, else `UNKNOWN`.\n\n**Keeping structural impact low:** I put the mapping alongside the existing derived-field expressions (`displayName`, `membershipTier`, etc.), matching the established idiom exactly rather than introducing a new class or service. The switch expression references `getCity()` once, keeping the changed method's complexity at CC 1, and I touched only the two files strictly required (the schema and the one mapper method) \u2014 no controller, service, or model changes.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity`, `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown`) and the full suite pass.",
